# TypeScript Rules

## Types
- Strict mode — no `any` unless unavoidable; prefer `unknown` + narrowing.
- Export prop types alongside components from `src/index.ts` when public.
- Domain types in `src/types/`; barrel-export from `src/types/index.ts`.

## Imports
- UI components: relative imports within `src/components/ui/`.
- Shared libs: `../../lib/theme-context`, `../../lib/typography`.
- Constants: `../../constants` or `@/` if tsconfig paths exist.

## Hooks & Services
- Side effects in hooks (`src/hooks/`), not in UI components.
- API types align with `src/lib/api-schema.ts` — single source of truth.
- Hook return shapes: explicit interfaces, stable referential callbacks via `useCallback`.

## Naming
- Components: PascalCase files (`button.tsx` → `Button`).
- Hooks: `use` prefix camelCase (`useApi.ts`).
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` in `constants/index.ts`.

## Examples
```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — typed variant union exported
export type ButtonVariant = "primary" | "secondary" | "outline";

// ❌ BAD — untyped string prop for known variants
variant?: string;
```
